WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.160
In step 6, we apply Pythagoras' theorem one last time, to the right-angled triangle GKX.

00:07.660 --> 00:13.520
We know the hypotenuse GX from step 3, and we know the base KX from step 5.

00:14.060 --> 00:18.880
Subtracting their squares and taking the square root gives us the vertical height GK.

00:19.440 --> 00:26.840
Finally, step 7. The vertical height G to K is the exact same length as H to F along the curve.

00:26.840 --> 00:30.460
Subtract the wheelbase L and front overhang K,

00:30.900 --> 00:35.140
and what remains is A to H, the exact extra space we need.

